{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A night of watchings for HaShem.</b> And afterwards it says, ״watchings for all the children of Israel throughout their generations,״ because the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel (Deuteronomy Rabbah 4:4): ״My lamp is in your hand and your lamp is in My hand; keep watch for Me and I shall keep watch for you — keep watch for the lamp of mitzvah and I shall keep watch for the lamp of Elohim, the soul of man that is in My hand.״ Now on this night Israel kept watch for the lamp of the mitzvah of the Paschal offering according to all its statutes, and the Holy One, blessed be He, kept watch over them and did not allow the Destroyer to enter their houses. And concerning this watch He said, ״A night of watchings for HaShem, to bring them out of the land of Egypt,״ and corresponding to Israel's watching of the mitzvot He said, ״watchings for all the children of Israel throughout their generations.״ But concerning the first occurrence He did not say ״throughout their generations,״ for the watching of the mitzvah of the Paschal offering alone was established for all generations, whereas protection from harmful forces was not established for all generations — for in Egypt alone did the Destroyer go forth to wreak destruction, and not for generations."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:40.279096322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}